const demandRows = [
  {
    signal: 'Recent vacancy volume',
    reality:
      'SSC CGL 2026 was notified for roughly 12,256 vacancies across departments. IBPS PO 2026 was notified for roughly 6,715 vacancies across 11 public sector banks, and SBI PO 2026 separately for roughly 1,500 vacancies. SSC currently offers the larger single vacancy pool of the three.',
  },
  {
    signal: 'Applicant pool size',
    reality:
      'SSC CGL routinely draws well over 25-40 lakh applicants nationwide because it is open to a very wide range of graduates chasing a wide range of departments. Bank PO exams (IBPS combined) typically draw a somewhat smaller applicant pool, commonly cited in the 15-25 lakh range, spread across fewer, more narrowly defined roles.',
  },
  {
    signal: 'Selection ratio',
    reality:
      'Both land in a similar rough zone — commonly cited estimates put SSC CGL selection odds near 1 in 250-300 applicants and IBPS PO odds near 1 in 300-350, though the exact ratio shifts every cycle with vacancy count and applicant volume. Neither exam is an easy tier to clear; both reward sustained, structured preparation over shortcuts.',
  },
];

const checkpointItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Biology',
    body: 'SSC rewards people who can hold a wide static-knowledge base (polity, history, geography, science facts) alongside solid quant and reasoning, and who do not mind a slower, more procedural office rhythm once selected. Bank exams reward people comfortable with fast, repetitive calculation under time pressure, plus comfort with customer-facing, target-driven work once selected, since PO roles carry deposit and loan targets from early on.',
    note: 'If the idea of daily sales-style targets genuinely drains you, that is a real signal toward SSC, not weakness. If slow-moving departmental process work would bore you fast, that leans toward banking.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Context',
    body: 'Both tracks typically need 4-8 months of serious, structured prep for a first realistic attempt, and most successful candidates do not clear on their first try — plan for 1-2 attempt cycles, not one shot. Bank exams run more frequent cycles across IBPS and SBI in the same year, which means more attempts per year if you fail one round. SSC CGL usually runs one main notification cycle a year, so a missed or failed attempt costs you a full year, not a few months.',
    note: 'If your family or financial runway cannot absorb 1-2 years of exam-focused prep without income, that constraint should weigh as heavily as which exam "suits your brain" better. Building a parallel, high-income skill — something you can freelance or monetise while you prepare — protects that runway and moves you toward financial freedom even before results are out.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
