  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not settle "SSC vs bank exams which to prepare for in India" from a relative's opinion or one viral
    salary screenshot for one more week.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Run yourself through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above, honestly, on paper.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then commit your next two to three months to the shared quant, reasoning, and English foundation
      while you decide, so no matter which exam family you finally choose, that time was not wasted.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Achieving earlier financial freedom through either track depends more on which posting-and-pace reality
    you can actually sustain for years, not just which exam looked easier to clear. Move toward that
    decision with <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    if you want a second opinion on your specific situation, or start with the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a>
    if you are still unsure which working rhythm genuinely fits you.
  </p>

